# The step of the dot product of one limb (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution"): one
# fused operation, s <- RN(x y + s). No product is rounded: the step is the addition of the state
# and of the exact product. Its elements come from arrays the program supplies; it only multiplies
# them, so rule R3 asks no guard of them (an entry kernel whose x and y enter from the program).
kernel:        dot_step_1
input:         stored s
input:         x
input:         y
output:        t
value:         s+x*y
ensures:       rounded t nearest
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/StepKernels.v dot_step_1_correct
ieee_bridge_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeSteps.v dot_step_1_ieee_bridge
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeFolds.v dot_step_1_ieee_lead
source:        the step of the fused dot product of one limb, s <- RN(x y + s) (milestone2.md)
license:       proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
ieee:          bridge

t = fma(x, y, s)
